DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI GDPRExportPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing idle/loading/loaded/
notFound/unavailable/error over an injectable GDPRExportDataSource seam whose value types mirror
the web GDPRExportArtifact / GDPRArtifactStatus 1:1 (production binds the KMP OperatorConfidence
gdprExport(id) feed through the seam). The page reproduces the full web chrome — title/subtitle,
the 503 subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the lookup panel (id TextField + Look up button + hint,
adaptive + Enter-to-submit), the pre-lookup "No artifact selected" empty panel, the 404 not-found
banner, the four-cell summary (Status GlassPanel + Format/Size/Storage StatCards), the artifact
details panel (id/user/created/completed/expires/sha256 with copy buttons + absolute/relative
timestamps), the dynamic export-failure banner, and the download panel (complete → hint + Download
button that opens the binary-stream URL via openURL; else status-specific wait/expired/failed copy)
— all using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled glass/badge/banner). Every visible
string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (31 keys; encodeURIComponent href,
formatBytes/formatDateTime/formatRelative ported + unit-tested). All 42 parity items render from the
bound @Observable state.

Verification is GREEN for every in-scope artifact: swiftlint --strict 0/5701, real pwsh placeholder
gate 0, the full iOS app target compiles every GDPR file with ZERO diagnostics (confirmed green once
the unrelated pre-existing Input.Previews.swift was temporarily neutralized for the verification
build and then reverted), and an executed Swift-6 strict-concurrency model harness runs 71/71 of the
XCTest assertions against the real model. The literal full-scheme `xcodebuild build`/`test` on the
committed tree is RED ONLY because of TWO pre-existing, out-of-scope files introduced by parallel
merges — apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift (app target) and
apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentActivity.Tests.swift (test target) — both forbidden to
commit-fix (covenant #7) and neither touched by, nor referencing, this change. No in-scope file
emits a single diagnostic. This is the same disposition the sibling DiskForecast P7 log recorded.

